# `entire review` Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Ship `entire review`, a command that runs the team's configured review skills against the current branch, lets the user fix findings or close with a git-visible review marker, and surfaces prior reviews so they aren't redundantly re-run.

**Architecture:** Tracking-first command — `entire` doesn't ship review prompts, it wraps existing skills (`/pr-review-toolkit:review-pr`, `/codex:adversarial-review`, etc.). Pending-review marker written to `.git/entire-sessions/` tags the next agent session as `Kind=review`. A new per-agent `Launcher` abstraction subprocess-spawns the agent (new capability — `entire` has historically been called *by* agents, not vice versa). Mid-session decision point is skill-driven (`/entire-review:finish`) relaying options through the agent's chat UI; Stop hook provides a `huh` TUI fallback. Decision outcomes: Fix (no commit, loopable), Close (empty commit with trailers on branch), Skip (no commit). Findings live in the session transcript; the empty commit's trailers point to the checkpoint.

**Spec:** [`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-20-entire-review-design.md`](../specs/2026-04-20-entire-review-design.md)

**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26, `github.com/spf13/cobra` (commands), `github.com/charmbracelet/huh` (TUI), `github.com/go-git/go-git/v6` (git operations), existing `entire` primitives: `trailers`, `settings`, `session`, `checkpoint`, `agent` registry.

---

